    "turn_text": "Just a cul-de-sac, since you mentioned it. There's been a couple of pieces now with them. There was a long piece the other day about the way that TikTok has survived the challenges that have been raised toward it, both by you and by many of your colleagues. There's this feeling on Capitol Hill that essentially TikTok's lobbying effort, especially among progressives, was very effective in shutting off the possibility that there would be a bipartisan push to either ban it or force it to be divested away from the Chinese Communist Party. Do you accept that frame of what's happened? Is there hope to ban TikTok just given that none of the security concerns that have been raised by you or other colleagues from my perspective have been addressed at all in terms of any kind of solution that would prevent it from being the kind of terrible force that it is in terms of propaganda and tracking American individuals?",
