    "turn_idx": 69,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, the only way to prevent, in my view, something happening in Taiwan before the end of this decade, which I think we're going to face some fork in the road there before the end of this decade, the only way to extend that to hopefully some other future time, you know, or maybe the dynamics would be different, is that China has believes that any conflict over Taiwan is one that they could potentially lose or get dragged down into a boondoggle. And so I do think that that is the reality and one that we have to make. I think that what I thought you were going to get at and I think you were somewhat is when Americans turn to us and say, okay, but explain to me again why my son or daughter is going to be killed defending Taiwan. I get it. It's bad China. And I don't think we've done enough for that because it's not just Taiwan. It's not that this island off the coast of China that China wants to take over. It's what two things the first is if they control it then all the territory the airspace and the territorial waters They will claim will basically make us a continental power will be driven out of Asia completely as regard the second So that's the first and then impact that would have on trade they would now control You know 70 60 70 percent of global commerce just you'd have to pay a toll if they wanted one just to go To get it to market because there were production still is even the production that moves out of China So that's number one, but the second is it would reorient the world If you're South Korea, if you're Japan, if you're Europe, if you're anybody on the planet, you would say, this is the first time in my lifetime, where a foreign country did whatever they wanted, America couldn't stop them. So the world has changed. I now know who the most powerful country in the world is, and it's not America. And therefore, we're going to have to start making decisions economic and otherwise on the basis of what the most China wants, not necessarily what America wants. And I think that would be none of us have ever lived in a world like that. of us have ever lived in a world in which America was not the most powerful country. And we have benefited from that in real ways.",
